Pommes Purée
Serves: 5
Prep: 15 min
Cook: 30 min
Total: 50 min
Source: Serious Eats, J. Kenji López-Alt
Equipment: Large pot, Potato ricer or food mill, Paring knife, Clean tea towel

Finish (heat, then keep warm): Add the butter in pieces, the cream and a good pinch of salt. Bring the cream to a **simmer** so the butter melts, then fold everything together. Loosen with stock or more cream. Season.
  Rice (combine): Peel while hot, holding them in a towel. Push through the ricer back into the empty pot.
    Boil (heat, ~30 min): Scrub. Cover with **cold** water, bring to a boil, then simmer until a knife slides in with **no resistance**. Drain; stand **5 min**.
      - 900 g = 2 lb | Potatoes | Yukon Gold type: medium-waxy, skin on
  - 115 g = 8 Tbsp | Unsalted butter
  - 355 ml = 1½ cups | Heavy cream | plus more as needed
  - 120 ml = ½ cup | Chicken stock | optional
  - to taste | Kosher salt & pepper
